<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.1.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01246</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.1.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7d9855ce-6416-4bd7-af16-dff08c44c3d1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.
</para>
<para>
  Simplify each expression using the appropriate property from the lesson. Double click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge.
</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_5bc25e84-3ebc-45a4-b6f7-6fbd0bb8aa7c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> \(f^2 \cdot f^6\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(f^{36}\)</para><para>\(f^4\)</para><para>\(f^{12}\)</para><para>\(f^8\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.2.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(f^8\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="d5986df5-4414-4eef-91a0-d11f39dab078" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> \(\frac{(-y)^6}{(-y)^3}\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((-y)^3\)</para><para>\((-y)^2\)</para><para>\((-y)^9\)</para><para>\((-y)^{18}\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.2.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \((-y)^3\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_09c7219f-b70c-4d73-ae66-7e7299eeb99b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> \((-4)^0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(0\)</para><para>\(4\)</para><para>\(1\)</para><para>\(-4\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.3.
     </para><para>The correct answer is 1.
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="ac9e29df-1ce0-4c16-897a-72c97c47e385" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> \(2^{-3}\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\( 8\)</para><para>\(-6 \)</para><para>\(\frac18\)</para><para>\( -\frac18 \)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(\frac18\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_347ae9cf-eb9c-4b6e-ac4e-3f0d83da8d33" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\frac{1}{(-t)^{-5}}\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\( t^4\)</para><para>\(t^5\)</para><para>\(\frac{1}{t^5}\)</para><para>\((-t)^5\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.3.

     </para><para>The correct answer is \((-t)^5\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="a33cdfaf-1aff-458f-b3e2-01d0c57f8eee" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((-\frac{m}{n})^{-3}\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(\frac{n^3}{m^3} \)</para><para>\(\frac{m^3}{n^3}\)</para><para>\(-\frac{n^3}{m^3}\)</para><para>\( -\frac{m^3}{n^3}\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.4.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(-\frac{n^3}{m^3}\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_1875b481-fb1c-4781-bc11-32b495e8b2b4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((d^3)^5\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\( d^{15}\)</para><para>\(d^8\)</para><para>\(d^5 \)</para><para>\(d^{-2}\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.4.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \( d^{15}\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="d043cfe7-16bd-4e49-a07d-bc62308ca3cc" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(( 5x^{-2})^3\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(\frac{ 125}{x^5}\)</para><para>\(5x\)</para><para>\(\frac{125}{x^6}\)</para><para>\(125x\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.4.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(\frac{125}{x^6}\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_811cfafd-0236-4b3b-816f-f9b65160ab88" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((\frac{7b^3c}{d^2})^2\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(\frac{d^4}{49b^6c^2}\)</para><para>\(\frac{7b^6c^2}{d^4}\)</para><para>\(\frac{49b^6c^2}{d^4}\)</para><para>\(\frac{49b^5c^2}{d^4}\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.4.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(\frac{49b^6c^2}{d^4}\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="bd146c8a-717e-498e-9add-216142ce0c5f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((\frac{3z^{-2}}{w^2})^{-2}\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(9z^4w^4\)</para><para>\(\frac{9w^4}{z^4}\)</para><para>\(\frac{w^4}{9z^4}\)</para><para>\(\frac{z^4w^4}{9}\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.1.4.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(\frac{z^4w^4}{9}\).
     </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
